 34SI  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34SI  H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34SI2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34SI c  2005Ti11,2006AnZW: a {+35}Al secondary beam at |?2 pps was produced via
 34SI2c  the fragmentation of a 78-MeV/nucleon {+36}S primary beam and selected 
 34SI3c  by the LISE3 spectrometer at GANIL. A total of 3.46|*10{+5} {+35}Al    
 34SI4c  ions were continuously implanted into an NE102A plastic scintillator   
 34SI5c  also for detecting |b. The implantation detector was sandwiched between
 34SI6c  two silicon detectors for monitoring beam and for veto, respectively.  
 34SI7c  Neutrons were detected using the TONNERRE array consisting of 19       
 34SI8c  plastic scintillator modules. |g rays were detected using two EXOGAM   
 34SI9c  clover modules and a LEPS detector. Measured E|g, I|g, E{-n}, I{-n},   
 34SIAc  |b|g-coin, |bn-coin, and |bn|g-coin. Deduced the decay scheme          
 34SIBc  consisting of {+35}Si and {+34}Si levels, {+35}Al T{-1/2}, decay       
 34SICc  branching ratios, log {Ift}, B(GT), and |b-delayed neutron emission    
 34SIDc  probability. Comparisons with shell-model calculations.                
 34SI c  2001Nu01,2002Nu02: a {+35}Al secondary beam at 8 pps was produced via  
 34SI2c  the fragmentation of a UC target with 1.4-GeV protons at ISOLDE, CERN  
 34SI3c  with subsequent surface-ionization and mass separation. {+35}Al ions   
 34SI4c  were collected onto a moving tape. |b particles were detected using a  
 34SI5c  thin cylindrical plastic scintillator, |g rays were detected using two 
 34SI6c  Ge detectors, and neutrons were detected using eight low-threshold     
 34SI7c  plastic scintillators. Measured E|g, I|g, E{-n}, I{-n}, |b|g-coin,     
 34SI8c  |g|g-coin, |bn-coin. Deduced the decay scheme consisting of {+35}Si and
 34SI9c  {+34}Si levels, {+35}Al T{-1/2}, decay branching ratios, log {Ift}, and
 34SIAc  |b-delayed neutron emission probability. Comparisons with shell-model  
 34SIBc  calculations.                                                          
 34SI c  Other experimental studies on {+35}Al T{-1/2} and |b-delayed neutron   
 34SI2c  emission probability: 2019Wa38, 2017Ha23, 1999YoZW, 1995ReZZ/2008ReZZ, 
 34SI3c  1989MuZU, 1989Le16, 1988MuZY, 1988Mu08, 1988DuZT, 1988BaYZ, 1987DuZU,  
 34SI4c  1987BaZI.                                                              
